## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Pinecone → Qdrant Migration**: This plan **replaces Pinecone** with a local Qdrant instance. Your existing Pinecone index (`jurisone-index`) will no longer be queried. **All PDFs in `source_docs/` must be re-ingested** into Qdrant. The `PINECONE_API_KEY` in `.env` will no longer be needed. Confirm you are okay with this data migration before proceeding.

> [!WARNING]
> **Docker Requirement**: Qdrant runs inside Docker. On your Windows machine, Docker Desktop must be running. The plan uses `docker run` to spin up the Qdrant container. If you prefer a different approach (WSL2, native binary), let me know.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Web Search for Unknown Queries**: When the RAG corpus has no relevant answer, the agent will hit external legal APIs/sites. The prioritized trusted sources are:
> - **Indian Kanoon API** (`indiankanoon.org`) — Indian case law (requires a free API key)
> - **SCC Online** (scraped via HTTP if no API) — secondary fallback
> - **Law Commission of India** official site — reports and acts
> 
> Do you have an Indian Kanoon API key? If not, the plan defaults to scraping their public search endpoint.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Contextual Retrieval cost**: The "Anthropic Contextual Retrieval" step calls Groq's Llama-3.3 **once per chunk** during ingestion. For 500 PDFs at ~20 chunks each = **~10,000 Groq API calls**. This is done only once at index-build time, but it will take significant time. Rate limits on Groq's free tier may require batching with delays.

